# Design Philosophy v1.0 (absolute priority)

NovaBrowser is a **professional web browser**, not a desktop app or React dashboard.

## Hierarchy (never invert)

1. Chromium / WebView  
2. Tabs  
3. Address bar  
4. Navigation  
5. Browser features  
6. Nova features  

**Browser first. Nova Ecosystem second** — like Chrome→Google, Edge→Microsoft, Arc→Spaces.

## Hard rules

- Web content owns ~**95%** of the window. Chrome must nearly disappear.
- If a UI element does not improve navigation, **delete it**.
- Home = **New Tab only** (logo, search, favorites, recents, workspace, Nova quick links). No dashboard, no widgets, no big panels.
- All Nova features are **`nova://` internal tabs** — never separate windows or app panels.
- Permanent chrome only: **tabs, toolbar, address bar, nav buttons, collapsible icon sidebar, WebView**.
- Sidebar: icons only, hover-expand, never wide, never the hero.
- Toolbar: Back, Forward, Refresh, Address Bar, New Tab, Profile, Ryuk — stop.
- Ryuk accompanies browsing; it is **not** the home experience and must not replace the browser.
- Do not build AI / NovaCloud / NovaDocs product features until the browser itself feels native and excellent.
- User must think: *"professional browser"* — never *"app with a browser inside"*.
- Forget Electron/React in the visual result: speed, elegance, fluidity, precision, simplicity.

## Examples

```text
✅ nova://settings opens as a normal tab in the WebView
❌ Settings as a sidebar panel, modal app screen, or separate window

✅ New Tab = quiet NTP like Chrome
❌ New Tab = dashboard with cards, sprint widgets, marketing panels
```
